+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope, Cancelling Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08 as one row covering two capabilities: changing a booked visit and cancelling one. [That ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) set the reopening rule — a future request touching the row proceeds only on an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, and never on the request's implication alone.
+
+The owner made that decision on 2026-08-16, at the intake for `REQ-VISITEDIT-001`. A visit can currently only be created, never corrected, and the two capabilities the row bundled no longer share a fate.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner decided otherwise, and the row's rationale only ever covered lifecycle state, which correcting a date and a description does not add.
+2. **Retire NG-5 entirely.** Open both correction and cancellation. Rejected: the owner kept cancellation out, and the 2026-08-08 rationale still holds for it.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 now declines cancelling a booked visit and nothing else. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, recorded as [`REQ-VISITEDIT-001`](../prd.md#req-visitedit-001).
+
+The sample still carries no visit lifecycle state: a corrected visit is the same visit with different values, so nothing distinguishes a cancelled visit from a kept one. Forward-only correction, established for owner and pet details, now covers visits too.
+
+Reaching the correction form is by direct address. The owner decided that the owner's record gains no link to it in this round, and named a follow-up request as the possible route to a visible entry point.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-5 is decided and narrowed; its row and the Non-Goals preamble both name this ADR.
+- Cancelling a booked visit remains declined, on the 2026-08-08 rationale. Reopening it needs a fresh owner decision recorded at intake.
+- The correction capability ships without a way to discover it. Whether that entry point arrives is one of the questions the narrowing leaves open in the PRD's [Open Questions](../prd.md#open-questions).
+- The 2026-08-08 ADR stands for NG-4 and for the cancellation half of NG-5; this ADR supersedes neither.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-visitedit-001) — the capability the narrowing admits.
